hampton 8th inst, with mdse and passengers, to Oelrichs\n& Co. Experienced westerly winds the entire passage. Aug\n16, 5:30 PM, lat 44 13, lon 48 55, passed steamship Helvetia,\nhence for Liverpool; 20th, 1:20[?] AM, lat 41 09, lon 65 56, passed\na French steamship bound E; same day, 2:30 AM, lat 41 07,\nlon 66 09, passed an Inman steamer, bound E.", "lineage_id": "herald:L2f90e8c179fab307", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-08-22/ed-1/seq-8/"}, {"mark": "9", "claim": "Spoken / sighted lat 41 37, lon 60 45 (14th)", "citation": "New York Herald, 17 August 1866, p. 8, col. 5", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_houseleek_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743555:1866081701:0670/3835,4484,981,278/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Steamship Denmark (Br), Thompson, Liverpool Aug 1, via\nQueenstown 2d inst, with mdse and 511 passengers, to Na-\ntional Steam Navigation Co. Had strong westerly gales up\nto the 11th inst, since light variable winds; 2d inst, passed\nsteamship Virginia, bound in; 3d, lat 51 10, lon 11 a steam-\nship, supposed the Persia, bound E; 8th, lat 47 55, lon 37\n10, bark Merrimac, bound E; 9th, lat 47 10, lon 37 10, ship\nPlymouth Rock and bark Josephine, bound E; 12th, lat 44\n10, lon 50, bark E S McNeil, of Boston, bound E; same day,\nBremen bark Meridian, bound E; 14th, lat 41 37, lon 60 45,\nsteamship Helvetia, bound E.", "lineage_id": "herald:Lf96021c9066013e0", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-08-17/ed-1/seq-8/"}, {"mark": "10", "claim": "Cleared New York (1866-08-10)", "citation": "New York Herald, 11 August 1866, p. 3, col. 1", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_houseleek_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743555:1866081101:0615/185,6657,934,364/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Steamship Helvetia (Br), Ogilvie, Liverpool—National Steam\nNavigation Co.", "lineage_id": "herald:L658f3faf1899fdde", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-08-11/ed-1/seq-3/"}, {"mark": "11", "claim": "In port Liverpool (25th)", "citation": "New York Herald, 11 September 1866, p. 9, col. 1", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_houseleek_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743555:1866091101:0893/92,3544,971,323/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Helvetia (s), Ogilvie, do;", "lineage_id": "herald:Ld8d8ed7abb0cb025", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-09-11/ed-1/seq-9/"}, {"mark": "12", "claim": "Cleared New York (1866-08-10)", "citation": "The Sun (New York), 11 August 1866, p. 4, col. 3", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:nn:batch_nn_brown_ver01:data:sn83030272:0020653607A:1866081101:0764/1439,121,707,274/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Helvetia,\nLiverpool", "lineage_id": "sun:Lc1aee44f54d738ae", "source": "sun", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030272/1866-08-11/ed-1/seq-4/"}, {"mark": "13", "claim": "Cleared New York (1866-08-10)", "citation": "New-York Tribune, 11 August 1866, p. 3, col. 6", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_delphi_ver03:data:sn83030214:00206530832:1866081101:0709/5047,4010,1016,120/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Steamship Helvetia (Br.), Ogilvie, Liverpool, National Steam Navi-\ngation Company.", "lineage_id": "tribune:Lb8ca31bd45648623", "source": "tribune", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030214/1866-08-11/ed-1/seq-3/"}, {"mark": "14", "claim": "Specie $10,000", "citation": "New York Herald, 12 August 1866, p. 2, col. 1", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-08-12/ed-1/seq-2/", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": null, "verbatim": "The shipment of specie by this day's steamers aggregated\n$86,175, of which the Ville de Paris took $58,000, the\nGermania $3,000, the City of Boston $15,175, and the\nHelvetia $10,000, making for the week $152,375.", "lineage_id": "herald:Lcab7b077f17dbd5d", "source": "herald"}], "aboard": {"specie": [{"text": "$10,000", "marks": ["14"]}], "passengers": [], "mails": [], "headlines": [], "mail": []}}